## Legacy Bakehouse LLC: Salmonella Strikes Again
Legacy Bakehouse LLC has announced a recall of multiple batches of their bagel crisps and pita chips. The recall stems from the use of a milk powder ingredient supplied by California Dairies that was itself recalled due to Salmonella contamination. Products affected include Butter Parsley Bagel Crisps, Parmesan & Herb Bagel Crisps, and others. These products were distributed across various channels, making it crucial for consumers to check their snacks and ensure they do not consume the affected items.

## Wawa Beverage Company: Allergy Alert
Close behind, Wawa Beverage Company has issued a recall for several of its bottled drinks, including Diet Iced Tea Lemon, Diet Lemonade, and Fruit Punch pints. The issue? An undeclared milk allergen. This oversight could pose a serious risk to consumers with milk allergies. Those affected should immediately stop consuming these products and return them to the point of purchase.

## Industry at Large: A Pattern of Neglect?
The recent spate of recalls once again highlights concerning practices in the food and beverage industry. Legacy Bakehouse and Wawa are not alone--2026 has already seen over 500 recalls, 152 of which were Class I, the most serious designation. Repeat offenders like Moonlight Packing Corporation and Albertsons Companies LLC continue to dominate the shame list, with numerous recalls due to critical safety violations.

## What Can Consumers Do?
Stay informed. Regularly check recall announcements and consider cutting ties with brands that repeatedly threaten consumer safety. Your health is worth the extra diligence.
